<region region-id="2" left="18.00" top="52.00" width="572.00" height="17.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="62.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge · common end-bent design (D-004).</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="3" left="18.00" top="75.00" width="572.00" height="43.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="85.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Mathcad edition of End_Bent_Backwall_Design.ipynb (calculation package 8e681afef630). Same inputs, equations and load combinations as the notebook; results should match its exported report (Section 12 lists the notebook values).</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="4" left="18.00" top="124.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="134.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Design Guidelines (SDG) and Structures Detailing Manual (SDM), January 2026.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="5" left="18.00" top="160.00" width="572.00" height="43.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="170.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Status: adopted CAD geometry reconciled 16 October; single centered #4 cheek mat at 10 in each way. Prerequisites remain pending (Section 12). Inputs are highlighted yellow; values for the plans are boxed.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="6" left="18.00" top="219.00" width="572.00" height="22.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="234.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">1. Design basis</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="7" left="18.00" top="247.00" width="572.00" height="212.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="257.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Tie-back straps in the backwall extend into the MSE fill and resist the end-bent horizontal load and overturning (D-014). Attachment requires total settlement of the soil above the cap bottom of 2 in or less (SDG 3.13.2.N.3).</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• The single pile row is effectively pinned (FBMP fixity 0.10), so moments are taken about the pile top O. The strap force is F = max(H, M / y_strap); the piles supply M / y_strap − H at O.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Vertical-load arms are measured from the pile line shifted 3 in toward the fill (placement tolerance, SDG 3.13.2.N.3). Permanent loads take the maximum factor on an overturning arm and the minimum on a stabilizing arm; live load and wind uplift take no stabilizing credit.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Pedestrian load only (D-015): 90 psf live-load surcharge. Backfill φ = 30°, δ = 0, γ = 115 pcf, active Coulomb pressure (D-016).</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• The landing slab bears on the backwall (D-017): 50 % of its load goes to gravity design with no stabilizing credit; its weight on the fill acts as an earth surcharge ES.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• The cheek walls retain no fill: wind only (D-018). The backwall is designed at the crown height with the strap 1.5 ft above the cap top (D-019).</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Backwall states: strap slack, soil causes fill-face tension; strap engaged, the strap pull causes span-face tension. Both are designed.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="8" left="18.00" top="477.00" width="572.00" height="22.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="492.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">2. Inputs</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="9" left="18.00" top="505.00" width="572.00" height="19.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="517.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 2" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Adopted CAD geometry and centered cheek mat</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="10" left="18.00" top="527.00" width="80.54" height="17.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="538.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="true" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="#ffff80" tag="">
